WEBVTT

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.740
Mitsuki.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:04.740
Mitsuki.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:05.560
Hm?

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.480
What are you doing?

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.400
You'll get in trouble with Onee-chan 
for spacing out like that.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.610
Let's be strong, Mitsuki.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.590
To protect Midgar... To protect our home.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.250
It's calling me.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.550
Wait, Miyako!

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.070
No!

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.440
Don't go!

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.340
Bye-bye.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:40.810
Miyako!

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:11.130
<b><i>Unlimited Fafnir</i></b>

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:23.410
<b>Basilisk Attacks</b>

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.700
Lisa, how many sugar cubes do you want?

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.320
I suppose I'll have one.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.120
Okay.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:31.400
How about you, Yuu?

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.140
No, I'm good.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.210
You drink black, don't you?

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.790
Morning, Iris.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:38.170
No!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.260
I read in a book that you should have

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.280
something sweet before you study.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.430
Really? Here, then.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.350
Hey! I was going to do it!

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:53.070
Now he can study really well today.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.440
Here, my fiancé.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.440
You know you can overburden a person

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.990
by pampering them too much.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:03.690
Okay.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:05.400
Sorry.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.560
You saved me, though.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.950
Thank you, Tear-san.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.580
Sure!

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.300
You're a good woman, Lisa.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.830
What is that supposed to mean?

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.980
You're not getting away 
with sexual harassment.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.510
No, I just mean I can respect you.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:27.350
Of course, you're pretty, too.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:28.680
Nice.

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.940
Mononobe, what about me?

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.100
What about me, Yuu?

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.720
Calm down, you two.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:41.440
We have a report from NIFL.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:45.030
The Basilisk that was moving 
out from the Saharan Desert

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.380
began crossing the ocean last night.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.560
The ocean's frozen?

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.550
It's salt.

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:53.210
Salt?

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.980
The Basilisk shoots red rays from its eyes.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:00.690
It's been determined that any target it hits

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:04.060
is turned into stone, ash, or salt.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:08.160
And it's headed straight for...

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.350
<i>It's after Tear.</i>

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.060
One glare, and Midgar is toast.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.670
It'll be much worse than 
the Hecatoncheir attack.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.960
We'll move to an uninhabited 
island near here by boat

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.640
and attract the Basilisk there.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:28.580
We've determined that 
the most effective strategy

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:31.290
would be to destroy the Basilisk 
and the island along with it.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.040
We're leaving tomorrow, huh?

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.000
Are you okay with being on a boat?

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.420
I mean, after your Dragon disaster...

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:47.110
Yeah, but I'll be okay.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:50.900
A lot of fun things happened on 
our last family vacation, too.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.170
It's a very precious memory to me.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:56.200
I could never hate traveling by boat.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.980
You always exceed my expectations.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.320
I'm not a girl you can 
measure with common sense.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.170
I want to

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:14.410
know more about you someday, though.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.590
I mean, if you don't want that...

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:20.540
It's okay.

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:27.280
I think I want you to know me, Mononobe.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.970
Boo-hoo...

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:43.780
My chaste maidens!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:46.040
They're leaving me.

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:49.380
Nothing could be more lonely.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.050
What a tragedy—

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.580
Excuse me! That goes over here!

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.460
NIFL is participating in the operation?

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:01.900
They've also come up with 
a plan to beat the Basilisk.

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.770
They're in preparations now.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:05.600
The more chances we have, the better.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.310
But is it true, Shinomiya-sensei?

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:12.780
That we have a member from 
outside the Brunhilde class?

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.430
To supplement our forces.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.900
We don't want to push the injured too much.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:22.120
She scored highest in a selection test.

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.480
I'm sure she'll be of help to you.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.620
Honoka...

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:32.430
I'm Tachikawa Honoka.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.340
You just got here,

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:36.960
and you scored highest? That's amazing.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:40.800
No, I'm still nothing 
compared to the rest of you.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.540
I'll work my hardest. I'm honored to join you.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.610
Yeah, glad to have you, Honoka-chan.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:47.760
You can ask me anything.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.090
Okay.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.780
Wow! I saw a dolphin over there!

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.600
Really?

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.560
Let's go, Mononobe, Honoka-chan.

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.660
What's up with you two?

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:07.970
I feel sick.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:08.990
So do I.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.570
My head's spinning.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.780
My stomach's churning.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.910
That's what happens when you read

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:18.330
or work on a computer inside a boat.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.830
Iris and the others are having fun outside.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.750
But I want to read.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:27.160
I'm almost at the part 
where they find the culprit.

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:30.200
Give it back.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.780
I'll give it back as soon as 
you're feeling less seasick.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.930
At this rate, you won't be able to eat,

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.310
and then you'll really get sick.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:42.850
I mean, if you're going to rest, 
I'll leave you alone.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:45.310
See you.

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.900
So that's the kind of person he is.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:57.330
That's why I can never forgive you.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.820
<i>Mitsuki... Lisa?</i>

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:00.860
Shh!

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.880
I don't need you to forgive me.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:07.030
What I did doesn't warrant forgiving.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.430
And that's why you're going 
to take responsibility

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.470
and shoulder my role in this fight, too?

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.880
I don't need your help.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.890
I apologize if I offended you.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.370
Mitsuki-san, do you insist that

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:23.940
the guilt of having killed Miyako-san, 
and the need to atone for it, is yours alone?

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.450
I won't push the blame for something 
I've done onto someone else.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:28.450
I really want to stop them, but...

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.400
Your words, if nothing else, are admirable.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.400
It's not something we can butt in on.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:34.610
But why don't you confront things a little more?

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.610
I'm confronting—

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:40.290
You don't even expect me to forgive you.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.250
Don't say things like that so lightly.

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:50.420
We're off to a pretty bad start.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.510
Knowing them,

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:55.740
I'm sure they'll do what 
they have to do, but...

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:57.880
<i>Two years ago,</i>

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.340
<i>Mitsuki killed her best friend, 
Shinomiya Miyako,</i>

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:02.390
<i>with her own hands after 
she'd turned into a Dragon.</i>

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.580
<i>And Lisa still...</i>

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:09.570
Hm?

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:11.920
Fyril?

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.610
Give me back my book.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.280
Your book?

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:17.950
Oh.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.080
Sorry.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.420
I forgot.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:24.280
Are you feeling better now?

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:25.650
I am.

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.290
I ate lots of dinner, too.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:30.750
See? My belly's full.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:32.280
Hey!

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:36.730
Wow, so this is enough to 
make a guy nervous, huh?

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.200
A-Are you teasing me?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.760
Now give it back.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.720
I want to know who committed the crime.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.050
I'll tell you, then.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:46.600
It was—

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.690
No!

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:51.630
Don't tell me!

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:52.520
Don't you dare!

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:57.410
I haven't actually read it!

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.760
I don't know who did it.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:02.820
You tricked me.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.580
Mean.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.440
I apologize,

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.630
but could you move?

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:16.720
That tickles!

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:18.190
No, stay still.

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.230
Why?

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:24.420
I want to write a book myself someday.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.680
And for that, I need to know a lot of things.

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.600
I'm doing this for research.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:35.780
Your heart's racing more than before.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.810
W-Well, yeah...

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.120
Anyone's heart would race 
if a cute girl touched them.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:45.610
Now you're hitting on me.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.540
I'm not hitting on you.

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:50.330
You shouldn't fall for me.

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:55.930
Not unless you're prepared 
to become a prince.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.140
Huh?

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:07.470
Guys' heart rates go up 
when cute girls touch them.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.080
But they don't necessarily 
want to hit on them.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:11.260
Interesting.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:12.900
Can we stop now?

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.730
I want you to hit on Lisa more.

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:17.980
What?

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.130
When have I hit on Lisa?

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.090
He's unaware.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:27.640
Are you done yet?

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:30.750
Yeah. It was pretty interesting.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.770
Could I do some research, too, then?

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:35.670
I want to ask about Lisa.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.110
Are you gathering information 
so you can hit on her?

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.360
No, not that.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:42.050
You've known Lisa for a 
long time, haven't you?

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:44.450
Yeah. We're in the same grade.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.000
What do you want to know?

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.150
Her measurements?

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:48.270
I'm being serious.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:50.820
I saw her

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:52.980
fighting with Mitsuki.

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:59.270
What do you think it'd take 
for Lisa to forgive Mitsuki?

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.500
You want to get them to make up?

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.200
I'd like to, if I can.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:05.730
Maybe I shouldn't be meddling, but...

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.130
No, I feel the same way.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.770
What they're doing is too unproductive.

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:12.800
Unproductive?

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:15.040
Yeah.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:19.340
They're making each other 
suffer for no real reason.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:21.800
They have a reason, don't they?

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:23.550
It's over Shinomiya Miyako.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:28.010
No, that's where you're already wrong.

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:31.140
Lisa doesn't resent Mitsuki at all.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.430
She doesn't?

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:43.320
What was it you wanted to talk about?

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:48.190
Oh, I want you to tell me 
about the three years

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.980
since you came to Midgar.

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:56.100
But so much has happened, I can't...

00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:01.300
Then tell me about the girl 
who was your best friend.

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:05.890
To be honest, I don't really 
want to talk about it.

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.100
I see.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:09.760
But...

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:15.100
If you'll do a favor for me, maybe I can try.

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:21.150
Is it okay if I hug you?

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.750
Nii-san.

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.600
This is really relaxing.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.740
I think I can do it now.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:39.980
It was on the day of a strong typhoon

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:42.960
that Miyako came to Midgar.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.010
Are you all right?

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.400
Don't mind me. Take care of the others.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:55.480
They're all exhausted from 
severe seasickness.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.740
But you'll catch a cold.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:02.520
Thanks. I'm Shinomiya Miyako.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.680
I was overwhelmed.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.990
She was pretty on the outside, too,

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:10.780
but more than that,

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:13.910
she gave off such a beautiful aura from within.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.450
She was dazzling.

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:17.910
Haruka-san's sister?

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:20.320
My sister's that famous?

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:22.940
The whole school admires her!

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:24.540
She's perfect in every way.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:26.380
I aspire to be like her.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:28.760
She'd be happy to hear that.

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:34.240
Miyako and I hit it off right away.

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:36.520
We became roommates.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:41.770
Kusanagi.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:46.070
She excelled at both academics 
and control over dark matter.

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:52.100
I felt rivalry towards her.

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:57.540
But she would wash away those feelings by just...

00:14:58.520 --> 00:15:01.020
I guess you could say... well...

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:04.500
She was really kind to me.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:08.240
Miyako was always attached to me.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.300
And I loved her, too.

00:15:14.170 --> 00:15:18.600
But in a way, perhaps that was her one flaw.

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:21.750
She gave me such high priority

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:24.190
that she made errors in judgment.

00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:25.690
Like that time.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:30.930
<i>Emergency alert! Emergency alert!</i>

00:15:30.930 --> 00:15:32.280
<i>Alert level A.</i>

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.370
<i>Type Purple.</i>

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:34.930
<i>Repeat.</i>

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:36.080
<i>Alert level A.</i>

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:37.580
<i>Type Purple.</i>

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:39.200
<i>Purple Kraken.</i>

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:42.960
It's here.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:46.720
The Kraken uses antimatter.

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:49.170
No defense would have any effect.

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:51.660
Then what do we do?

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:57.040
It's calling me.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.020
Miyako-san, what are you talking about?

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:03.550
Your Ryumon...

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:04.650
Why?

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:13.200
Miyako!

00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:27.230
Where are we?

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:29.300
Run.

00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:34.620
I'm the one it's after.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:35.890
But don't worry.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.560
I'll protect you, Mitsuki.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:40.540
What are you talking about?

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.580
Miyako! No!

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:44.960
Don't go!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:47.980
Bye-bye.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:51.250
Miyako!

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:58.650
Two of them?

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:01.100
Miyako...

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:05.320
That's her?

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:09.560
Miyako...

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:11.950
Miyako...

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.440
<i>It'll be all right, Mitsuki.</i>

00:17:19.940 --> 00:17:21.440
<i>I'm with you.</i>

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:23.640
<i>Draw your bow,</i>

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.440
<i>and aim.</i>

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.650
<i>You can do it, Mitsuki.</i>

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:53.220
Was that...

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:56.170
Antimatter?

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.390
Me?

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:03.100
<i>Fire, Mononobe Mitsuki!</i>

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:08.980
<i>You should be able to destroy 
the other one with that attack.</i>

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:11.150
But that's Miyako!

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:13.370
You're the only one who can do it.

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:14.750
This is an order.

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:16.180
It's not by your will.

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:17.470
It's my will.

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:20.250
I'll take full responsibility.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:24.570
<i>Now, fire.</i>

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:26.330
<i>Fire!</i>

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.330
<i>Mitsuki!</i>

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:31.100
<i>If you don't, I'll...</i>

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.680
<i>I love you, Mitsuki.</i>

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:58.070
Miyako!

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:12.780
Thank you.

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:16.880
Hey,

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:23.310
have you ever asked Lisa to forgive you?

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.100
I never have.

00:19:25.520 --> 00:19:28.770
What I did was...

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:32.300
Why don't you consider a 
little how Lisa feels, too?

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:37.100
It's tiring being angry

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:41.530
or bitter over something for so long.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:46.120
Why don't you give Lisa an 
opportunity to forgive you?

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:51.330
Lisa-san cared about Miyako, too.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:53.760
She has a right to be angry at me.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:57.330
Don't you want her to forgive you?

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:58.090
That's not it.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:03.360
Then go ask her tomorrow what 
it'd take for her to forgive you.

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:06.100
This is an order, as your brother.

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:09.550
What the heck?

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:11.800
Do you really not want to?

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.060
I will.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:20.110
I don't want you to think I'm running away.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:23.280
That's my poor loser of a sister.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:24.860
Jeez.

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:27.060
Say what you will.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.580
Mononobe Yuu.

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:41.340
You said something to Mitsuki-san, didn't you?

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:42.870
Uh...

00:20:42.870 --> 00:20:44.090
I knew it.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.320
Otherwise there's no way she would have

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:50.230
asked what it'd take for me to forgive her.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:54.060
I just told her to consider 
how you feel, too.

00:20:54.650 --> 00:20:57.900
You don't really resent Mitsuki, do you?

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:04.570
It was Fyril-san, wasn't it?

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:07.410
She's meddling, too?

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:14.000
If it will lessen Mitsuki-san's guilt,

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:17.960
I'll continue to be her punishment.

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:22.970
You really are a good woman.

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.580
But it's been two years.

00:21:25.580 --> 00:21:26.910
I think that's long enough.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:27.710
But—

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:31.120
Mitsuki's already decided 
how to confront her guilt.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:34.020
So I want you to think about 
how you'll forgive her.

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:37.950
She'll meet any condition you ask.

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:42.860
You're very partial toward 
your sister, aren't you?

00:21:43.390 --> 00:21:47.950
Fine, then. I'll think of an 
impossibly difficult condition.

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.700
It'll be your fault if she can't handle it.

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:57.700
Maybe I went too far.

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:05.990
That's the volcanic island.

00:23:39.810 --> 00:24:09.670
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:43.810
That felt awful,

00:23:43.810 --> 00:23:45.760
but we made it to the volcanic island.

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.690
There's a lot we need to do here.

00:23:49.290 --> 00:23:51.420
Is this the island map?

00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:54.460
Huh, there's a hot spring.

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:57.760
Oh, first, I have to do that thing.

00:23:58.620 --> 00:24:02.990
Next time on <i>Unlimited Fafnir</i>: 
"Front Line in Distant Waters."

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:07.070
Mononobe-kun, this time is for you.

00:24:07.070 --> 00:24:08.480
Look forward to it.

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:19.890
<b>Illustration: karory</b>
